WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:11.224
In this video, we'll take the workshop
setup back out, with one prompt or by hand.

2
00:00:11.224 --> 00:00:14.802
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.168
In a new chat, paste the uninstall
prompt from the site, and send it.

4
00:00:20.252 --> 00:00:23.467
The agent reads the list the
setup kept of what it added.

5
00:00:24.867 --> 00:00:28.410
It shows you everything it
will remove, the skills,

6
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.786
the checklist and the workshop
folder, and waits for your okay.

7
00:00:32.786 --> 00:00:33.342
Say yes.

8
00:00:35.841 --> 00:00:40.656
It removes them, checks they're gone,
and tells you what's left for you.

9
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:45.067
It leaves three things to you:
the workshop settings,

10
00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:47.816
your GitHub repo and your Copilot plan.

11
00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:52.835
To remove the settings,
open your user settings as JSON.

12
00:00:53.535 --> 00:00:56.527
Select the 16 workshop lines and delete them.

13
00:01:01.136 --> 00:01:03.948
Save, then restart VS Code Insiders.

14
00:01:08.882 --> 00:01:14.265
Or do it yourself, with the guide
on the site, on a Mac or on Windows.

15
00:01:14.265 --> 00:01:17.034
It's eight steps, about ten minutes.

16
00:01:17.882 --> 00:01:21.608
First, look at the setup's
own record of what it added.

17
00:01:21.824 --> 00:01:23.626
Delete the workshop folder.

18
00:01:23.626 --> 00:01:28.763
That takes out the case study,
the workshop files and the tools it installed.

19
00:01:30.261 --> 00:01:35.326
Remove the workshop skills from your skills
folder, and put back any you had before.

20
00:01:39.416 --> 00:01:42.005
Delete the setup checklist's two folders.

21
00:01:45.491 --> 00:01:49.984
If you turned on the weekly taste
automation, delete it in Automations.

22
00:01:52.394 --> 00:01:55.429
Remove the workshop settings,
the way you just saw.

23
00:01:58.771 --> 00:02:03.776
If the setup installed Git, Node or
the GitHub CLI, remove the line that

24
00:02:03.776 --> 00:02:08.571
helps your computer find them,
and the GitHub sign-in helper for Git.

25
00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:13.702
Your Excalidraw repo on GitHub
is yours. Keep it, or delete it.

26
00:02:14.151 --> 00:02:18.827
Last, cancel the free month before
it renews, so you're not charged.

27
00:02:19.180 --> 00:02:22.220
The setup never touched anything
you had before the workshop.
